    "abstract": "Magnetic compounds with noncentrosymmetric chiral crystal structures and spin-frustrated lattices are renowned for their complex magnetic ordering and diverse correlated phenomena. In this report, we present a comprehensive study of the chiral and triangular lattice magnetic system Ni2ScSbO6, which exhibits incommensurate spin-density wave antiferromagnetic long-range ordering at a temperature of TN = 62 K, as revealed by bulk magnetization, specific heat, and neutron diffraction studies. In contrast to its isostructural materials Ni3TeO6 and Ni2InSbO6, Ni2ScSbO6 does not exhibit ferroelectric ordering, potentially due to its unique sinusoidal spin-density wave magnetic ordering. The onset of this magnetic ordering is closely linked to a series of intriguing phenomena occurring at TN , including prominent magnetodielectric coupling manifested by a sharp λ-like dielectric peak, substantial spin-phonon coupling characterized by anomalous phonon softening, and a remarkable volume magnetostriction effect revealed by highresolution synchrotron X-ray diffraction studies. These phenomena demonstrate an intricately coupled behaviour, highlighting Ni2ScSbO6 as a unique and interesting material.",
